   no sign change, no zero: for (H)-profiles the symmetry line carries no zeros at all

=== 3. the endpoint pinch, for the lacunary family too? ===
        k dist to [0,1] on the line           2*pi/k
       32           0.9354342059     0.1963495408
       64           0.1790357893     0.0981747704
      128           0.0372937744     0.0490873852
      256           0.0185378100     0.0245436926
   for the lacunary family the nearest zero to the real axis is the one at Re q = 1/2,
   and it is closer than 2*pi/k : the fair coin is the pinch point, not the endpoints

=== 4. what this says, stated so it can be attacked ===
   The Lee-Yang zeros of Gamma^(q) separate the profiles on which the annealed count is
   asymptotically exact from the one on which it is not, and they do it at the fair coin.
   FALSIFIER 1: exhibit a profile satisfying (H) whose zeros approach q = 1/2.
   FALSIFIER 2: exhibit a profile violating (H) whose zeros stay away from q = 1/2.
   Neither is ruled out here.  Two families are two families.
